<%# The inbox. Subscribed to the viewer's inbox stream: new activity anywhere
    triggers a Turbo 8 page refresh (morphing, scroll-preserving), which
    re-renders this page per-viewer — see Chats::Broadcasts for why refreshes
    beat surgical row patches here.

    The chats--refresh-inbox wrapper heals a MISSED refresh broadcast: Action
    Cable has no replay, so a broadcast sent while the socket was down (tab
    backgrounded, network blip) would leave the inbox stale until the user
    navigated. The controller re-runs the same page refresh on cable reconnect
    and on return-to-visible. It needs to wrap the <turbo-cable-stream-source>
    that `turbo_stream_from` renders so it can observe its `connected`
    attribute as the heartbeat. %>

<%# The OTHER inbox-staleness case, distinct from a missed broadcast: a Turbo
    RESTORATION visit (browser back / Hotwire Native stack pop) serves the
    inbox's cached snapshot with no GET. Open a chat from a profile, send a
    message, tap back — the snapshot cached before the chat existed comes back
    and the new conversation is missing until you navigate away and return.
    The reconciler above can't help (it only fires on reconnect / visibility,
    not on a restore visit). `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` makes the inbox
    uncacheable, so a restore visit re-fetches from the network and is always
    fresh — on the web AND in Hotwire Native, whose back-pop issues a Turbo
    `.restore` visit that honors this. Requires the host layout to
    `yield :head` (the Rails convention); harmless no-op otherwise.
    https://turbo.hotwired.dev/handbook/building#opting-out-of-caching %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
<% end %>
<%= chats_styles %>
<div data-controller="chats--refresh-inbox">
  <%= turbo_stream_from chats_current_messager, :chats_inbox %>
</div>

<div class="chats chats-inbox">
  <header class="chats-inbox__header">
    <h1 class="chats-inbox__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.title") %></h1>
  </header>

  <% if Chats.config.search %>
    <%= form_with url: conversations_path,
          method: :get,
          class: "chats-search",
          role: "search",
          data: {
            controller: "chats--debounced-submit",
            action: "input->chats--debounced-submit#queue search->chats--debounced-submit#queue",
            "chats--debounced-submit-delay-value": 250,
            turbo_frame: "chats_inbox_results"
          } do %>
      <%= search_field_tag :q, params[:q],
            placeholder: t("chats.inbox.search_placeholder"),
            class: "chats-search__input",
            autocomplete: "off" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= turbo_frame_tag "chats_inbox_results", target: "_top" do %>
    <% if @conversations.any? %>
      <ul class="chats-inbox__list">
        <% @conversations.each do |conversation| %>
          <%= render "chats/conversations/conversation_row",
                conversation: conversation,
                viewer: chats_current_messager,
                unread_count: @unread_counts.fetch(conversation.id, 0) %>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% elsif params[:q].present? %>
      <div class="chats-empty">
        <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.no_results_title") %></p>
        <p class="chats-empty__hint"><%= t("chats.inbox.no_results_hint", query: params[:q]) %></p>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="chats-empty">
        <span class="chats-empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
        <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_title") %></p>
        <p class="chats-empty__hint"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_hint") %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
